# Keep the build context small and predictable.
#
# Dockerfile.pump does `COPY . .` with the repo root as context. Unignored,
# that is 5.5 GB on a working checkout — almost entirely cv/.venv (5.4 GB) —
# uploaded to the daemon before the build starts. CI is unaffected because it
# builds from a fresh clone; this is for local builds.
#
# It also matters for safety. Nothing sensitive reaches a shipped layer today
# (the final stage is FROM scratch and copies only the binary), but with
# `COPY . .` in the context, adding one COPY to a final stage is all it would
# take to publish local calibration captures or an env file to a public
# registry.

# Virtualenvs and Python build artefacts
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# VCS and tooling
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude

# Docs, screenshots and design material — none of it ships in an image
docs/
assets/
*.md

# Local model weights, calibration output and captures. Large, machine
# specific, and in the case of calibration, images of the room.
cv/models/
cv/calibration/
cv/prototypes/
cv/snapshots/
clips/

# Node tooling, if a local install ever appears
node_modules/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
